WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.133
-Attorney General
Merrick Garland announced

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:05.467
that he has appointed
a special counsel to oversee

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:07.400
the Justice Department's
investigations

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.868
of former
President Donald Trump

00:00:08.868 --> 00:00:11.701
and Trump has responded
by spending the last few days

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:14.534
whining that he is a victim
of political persecution.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.667
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:21.000
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.901
If you watch this show,
I'm sure you're aware

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.701
that Donald Trump announced
his third run

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:25.934
for the presidency last week.

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:27.701
In fact, if you watch this show

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.400
and, somehow,
you are unaware of that fact,

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.200
I would like to know
who you are.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.734
[ Laughter ]
I mean, this show is basically
the local news Santa Tracker,

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.901
but for Donald Trump.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.701
Point is,
you know he's running again,

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.334
but I still feel like
I might have to tell you

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:42.434
because it just seems
different, this time.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:45.033
For example, you may have
noticed that Trump's message

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.834
and even his demeanor
during his announcement

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:50.000
were quite a departure
from his first run back in 2016.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.133
Let's compare the central themes

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:55.200
of his first campaign from 2016
and this one.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.200
-I, alone, can fix it.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.367
I'm a victim.

00:00:58.367 --> 00:00:59.367
I will tell you.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.167
[ Laughter ]
I'm a victim.

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.968
-Quite the hero's journey.

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:04.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:06.968
He went
from "I, alone, can fix it"

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.734
to "I am a victim."

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:12.367
[ Laughter ]
That's like Superman flying
into a bank to stop a robbery,

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:15.334
only to come out with his
underpants on his head, crying,

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.701
"There were like five bad guys
in there.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:18.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:21.067
Why didn't anyone give me
a heads-up?"

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.934
Seriously, who is this message
supposed to appeal to?

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:27.033
Does Trump think people
will vote for him

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.667
because they feel bad for him?

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.534
I wouldn't be surprised
if his first campaign ad was one

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:33.634
of those ASPCA commercials,

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.801
[ Laughter ]
except, instead of your
money going to animals,

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:36.734
it goes to him.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.501
[ As Trump ]
In the arms of --

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.133
[ Laughter ]
In the arms of an angel.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.534
So true, so true.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.601
[ Laughter ]
You know, I met an angel, once.

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.868
He was an ethereal being
of pure energy and light.

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:47.634
Big angel, strong angel.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:48.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:51.334
Came up to me,
tears pouring down

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:53.534
[ Laughter ]
his glowing, radiant angel face

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:54.667
and he knelt down next to me

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.100
and he laid his hand
upon my shoulder

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.400
and he said to me,
"Donald, wake up.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.234
It's Rudy. You fell asleep
during the meeting."

00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:00.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:03.334
And I said, "I was wondering why
my angel smelled

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:04.534
like Scotch farts."

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:05.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.100
Anyway, click here to donate.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.634
Someone get this [bleep] dog
away from me.

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:10.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.267
By the way,
if you thought the contrast

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:14.000
between those two speeches
was striking,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.100
you're not the only one.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.467
Even Fox Business noticed
the difference,

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:20.434
during an interview with Trump's
daughter-in-law Lara Trump,

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.267
who seemed caught off-guard
by the question.

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:25.567
-I have to say that there wasn't
a great reception

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.267
to the speech last night.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:30.934
Not a single elected
Republican official was there.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.234
How do you feel about it?

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:34.701
You were there, so, I'm sure
you're very supportive

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.167
of your father-in-law...
-[ Nervous laugh ]

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:40.100
...but those of us on the
outside, looking at it,

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.534
it didn't seem
as he got the old magic.

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:43.234
You know what I mean?

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:46.868
-Oh, well, I highly
disagree with that.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.400
-Wow. If you're a member
of the Trump family,

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.334
you are not used to getting
tough questions on Fox Business.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:54.834
[ Laughter ]
That's like Ryan Gosling getting
grilled on the red carpet.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:56.133
"Really, Ryan, a white tux?

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:58.434
Are you attending the
Golden Globes, or catering them?

00:02:58.434 --> 00:02:59.167
Ya burnt!"

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:02.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.300
You could tell
she was unprepared

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.167
for such a hostile reception

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.968
because she did
that awkward chuckle

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:10.234
halfway through the question,
like your mom

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:12.834
passive-aggressively fighting
with your dad at Thanksgiving.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:15.234
"Honey, is this turkey
intentionally dry?

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:18.567
[ Laughing ]
Because it's so well done."

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:19.701
That's funny, Richard.

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:21.000
The way you were flirting
with Maria,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.033
I assumed you like
dried-up old birds.

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:26.567
[ Laughter and oohs ]

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:28.467
Richard, ya burnt.

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:32.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:34.501
But that is the core
of Trump's message

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:37.400
and of GOP ideology --
performative victimhood.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.968
And that fake victimhood only
got more ridiculous on Friday,

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:41.467
when the attorney general,
Merrick Garland,

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:43.968
announced that he was appointing
a special counsel

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:46.601
to oversee the department's
investigations of Donald Trump.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.567
-I'm here today to announce
the appointment

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:50.100
of a special counsel

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.434
in connection with two ongoing
criminal investigations

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:56.667
that have received
significant public attention.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:59.200
The first, as described
in court filings

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.033
in the District of Columbia,

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:02.167
is the investigation

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:05.300
into whether any person
or entity

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.968
unlawfully interfered
with the transfer of power

00:04:08.968 --> 00:04:11.834
following the 2020
presidential election

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:15.133
or the certification of the
Electoral College vote held

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:18.601
on or about January 6, 2021.

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:21.501
The second is
the ongoing investigation

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:25.501
involving classified documents
and other presidential records,

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.167
as well as the possible
obstruction

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.667
of that investigation,

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:31.467
referenced and described
in court filings,

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:34.567
in a pending matter in the
Southern District of Florida.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.400
-I like how he never says
Trump's name, once,

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.868
in that clip, but you know
who he's talking about.

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:42.067
[ Laughter ]
Garland couldn't have been any
more specific, if he tried.

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.667
[ As Garland ]
I am here today to announce the
appointment of a special counsel

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.100
in connection
with an investigation

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.534
into whether
presidential records

00:04:47.534 --> 00:04:49.300
were illegally retained
by any individual,

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.734
specifically sweaty, loudmouthed
real estate moguls from New York

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:54.601
[ Laughter ]
who own chintzy resorts
in Palm Beach

00:04:54.601 --> 00:04:56.601
and don't know how to close
a [bleep] umbrella.

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:59.133
[ Laughter and applause ]
It's back, baby!

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:00.868
The umbrella video is back!

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:03.367
You run again, we play
the umbrella video again.

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:05.834
[ Laughter and applause ]
Them's the rules!

00:05:05.834 --> 00:05:08.000
So, if you're keeping track
at home,

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.133
we're now in our second
special counsel looking

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:12.701
into whether Donald Trump,
a notoriously corrupt

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:15.067
criminal authoritarian
dip[bleep], broke any laws.

00:05:15.067 --> 00:05:16.801
And by the way, the special
counsel Garland appointed is

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:19.100
a guy named Jack Smith,
who, by all accounts,

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.767
and also by his name,

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:23.300
another no-nonsense,
tough-as-nails prosecutor

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.067
who will follow the facts
and won't be intimidated,

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:27.067
which is the same thing
they said about Robert Mueller,

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:29.200
which is cool, I guess,
but where did that get us?

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.601
I mean, Mueller outlined
ten different allegations

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:34.467
of obstruction of justice,
not to mention actual proof

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.033
that Trump's campaign
openly welcomed

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.400
and encouraged foreign
interference in the election

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.701
and then all Trump had to do
was lean into the mic and say...

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:42.701
-Wrong.

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:45.567
[ Laughter ]
-...and that was it.

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:47.767
By the way, that's what we here
at "Late Night" call

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:48.968
another classic vid.

00:05:48.968 --> 00:05:51.100
[ Laughter ]
[ Electronic voice ]

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.901
[ Vuvuzela blasts ]

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:55.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.701 --> 00:05:56.767
Okay.

00:05:56.767 --> 00:05:57.434
Yeah.

00:05:57.434 --> 00:06:00.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:04.033
I think they had time
to read it.

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:04.868
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:06.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:07.601
Now, with all that said,

00:06:07.601 --> 00:06:10.133
the situation has changed,
this time,

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:12.634
so, there's reason
to be cautiously optimistic

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:14.033
that, maybe,
things will be different.

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:15.400
A former member
of Mueller's team,

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:16.534
Andrew Weissmann, tweeted...

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:32.267
Okay, so, how long should we
give him, a week?

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:34.334
[ Laughter ]
Based on the evidence
that's already public,

00:06:34.334 --> 00:06:35.701
he could've interrupted Garland

00:06:35.701 --> 00:06:37.801
halfway through the press
conference introducing him.

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:39.234
We're going to give Jack
the time he needs --

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:41.534
"Actually, America,
can I just jump in?

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:42.701
I think I'm good to indict."

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:44.767
[ Laughter ]
I mean, did you see that photo

00:06:44.767 --> 00:06:47.000
of all the top secret documents
spread out on his floor?

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.067
[ Laughter ]
Pretty sure he left
his fingerprints

00:06:49.067 --> 00:06:50.434
in the ketchup blots.

00:06:50.434 --> 00:06:51.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:53.167
Anyway, it won't surprise you
to learn

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.300
that Trump immediately
started complaining

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.534
about the appointment
of a special counsel

00:06:57.534 --> 00:07:01.167
at a gala at Mar-A-Lago
last week after the news broke

00:07:01.167 --> 00:07:04.634
and, in usual Trump fashion,
he just went on and on about it.

00:07:04.634 --> 00:07:06.534
Also, please enjoy the fact
that he's whining

00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:08.400
about all this stuff
while also dressed

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.267
like the piano player
at a Long Island steakhouse.

00:07:11.267 --> 00:07:12.400
-I want to address

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.067
[ Laughter ]
the appalling announcement today

00:07:14.067 --> 00:07:18.067
by the egregiously corrupt
Biden administration

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:20.200
and their weaponized
Department of Justice.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.934
Would you like me
to talk about that?

00:07:21.934 --> 00:07:23.400
This is a rigged deal,

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:26.067
just as the 2020 election
was rigged,

00:07:26.067 --> 00:07:28.000
and we can't let them get
away with it.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:33.634
I was tried on the fake
impeachment hoax on January 6th

00:07:33.634 --> 00:07:35.400
and isn't this sort of like
double jeopardy?

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.033
In the old days, they used
to call it double jeopardy.

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:40.868
[ Laughter ]
Why aren't they

00:07:40.868 --> 00:07:44.434
investigating all of the other
presidents that preceded me?

00:07:44.434 --> 00:07:45.467
-[ As Trump ]
Alright, enough talking.

00:07:45.467 --> 00:07:47.601
♪ It was 5:00 ♪

00:07:47.601 --> 00:07:50.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:50.601 --> 00:07:51.968
Oh, and also, all?

00:07:51.968 --> 00:07:55.067
You want them to investigate all
of the other presidents?

00:07:55.067 --> 00:07:56.334
[ Laughter ]
All 44?

00:07:56.334 --> 00:07:57.501
[ As Trump ]
Why aren't they investigating

00:07:57.501 --> 00:07:59.734
William "The Refrigerator" Taft

00:07:59.734 --> 00:08:02.501
[ Laughter ]
or Grovelin' Grover Cleveland

00:08:02.501 --> 00:08:03.634
or Lyin' Lincoln?

00:08:03.634 --> 00:08:05.534
Lyin' Abe Lincoln.
What's under that hat?

00:08:05.534 --> 00:08:06.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.934 --> 00:08:08.701
I've said it for years --
look under the hat.

00:08:08.701 --> 00:08:10.868
Nobody listened to me.
Nobody looked under the hat.

00:08:10.868 --> 00:08:12.300
You don't think he
smuggled documents

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.167
out of the White House
in that giant hat?

00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:17.267
[ Laughter ]
I guarantee you, if you lifted
that hat off his dumb head,

00:08:17.267 --> 00:08:20.767
you'd find an old Civil War
document that says...

00:08:20.767 --> 00:08:22.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:23.767
In defense of Trump,

00:08:23.767 --> 00:08:25.334
I do think it must've been
a little suspicious

00:08:25.334 --> 00:08:28.534
when Lincoln started wearing
those giant hats one day.

00:08:28.534 --> 00:08:29.934
[ Laughter ]
I don't want to spread
any rumors, but come on.

00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:32.367
If your buddy Dale suddenly
started showing up to work

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:33.601
in a stovepipe hat...

00:08:33.601 --> 00:08:34.734
[ Laughter ]

00:08:34.734 --> 00:08:36.200
...you would think
something was up.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.067
[ Whispering ]
"Psst! Hey, guys, want to know

00:08:38.067 --> 00:08:40.467
who took all the free pizza
from the conference room?

00:08:40.467 --> 00:08:42.968
[ Laughter ]

00:08:42.968 --> 00:08:44.133
Dinner for a week, baby!"

00:08:44.133 --> 00:08:46.634
Get outta here, Dale!

00:08:46.634 --> 00:08:47.834
We all know it was you.

00:08:47.834 --> 00:08:49.701
You stink like pepperoni!

00:08:49.701 --> 00:08:52.467
[ Laughter ]

00:08:52.467 --> 00:08:53.701
Now, as we told you last week,

00:08:53.701 --> 00:08:55.701
Trump's announcement speech
was so boring,

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.834
even Fox News cut away from it
before it was over.

00:08:57.834 --> 00:09:00.434
And then on Friday,
just to add insult to injury,

00:09:00.434 --> 00:09:01.767
the same thing happened
to Trump again,

00:09:01.767 --> 00:09:04.067
except, this time,
it was on C-SPAN.

00:09:04.067 --> 00:09:06.367
-In Afghanistan,

00:09:06.367 --> 00:09:10.000
when I was in charge,
we didn't have one killing.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.100
Think of it.
In 18 months,

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:14.033
not one of our soldiers
were killed.

00:09:14.033 --> 00:09:15.367
And then you look at Chicago

00:09:15.367 --> 00:09:16.367
and you look
at other [indistinct].

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:20.334
[ Applause ]

00:09:20.334 --> 00:09:22.167
-Former President Trump
has moved on

00:09:22.167 --> 00:09:23.634
[ Laughter ]
to other topics.

00:09:23.634 --> 00:09:24.934
We'll take this opportunity

00:09:24.934 --> 00:09:26.868
to move on
with our program schedule.

00:09:26.868 --> 00:09:29.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.834
I would say C-SPAN
just Ya Burnted Trump,

00:09:31.834 --> 00:09:33.200
but they can't afford
the graphics.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:36.234
[ Laughter ]

00:09:36.234 --> 00:09:38.234
Even C-SPAN cut away!

00:09:38.234 --> 00:09:39.334
This is the network famous

00:09:39.334 --> 00:09:41.200
for showing wide shots
of empty chairs

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.601
and even they were like,
"This [bleep] is boring."

00:09:43.601 --> 00:09:44.634
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.634 --> 00:09:46.167
You know how bad
your speech has to be

00:09:46.167 --> 00:09:47.968
for C-SPAN to cut away from it?

00:09:47.968 --> 00:09:49.567
You know what their
program schedule was

00:09:49.567 --> 00:09:50.734
that they had to get back to?

00:09:50.734 --> 00:09:52.801
An old man silently doing
the crossword by himself

00:09:52.801 --> 00:09:54.367
for six hours
and then falling asleep.

00:09:54.367 --> 00:09:55.634
[ Laughter ]

00:09:55.634 --> 00:09:57.167
If our laws are to have
any meaning at all,

00:09:57.167 --> 00:09:58.834
then, obviously,
Donald Trump should be indicted.

00:09:58.834 --> 00:10:01.033
It shouldn't take six years
and multiple special
counsels to do

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:03.434
and we certainly can't wait
for the Republican Party

00:10:03.434 --> 00:10:05.400
to finally decide if they're
willing to turn on Trump

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:08.067
because, while Republicans
are engaged in a family feud,

00:10:08.067 --> 00:10:10.534
trying to decide
if the price is right,

00:10:10.534 --> 00:10:12.133
our democracy is very much in...

00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:13.601
-Jeopardy.
-Oh, boy.

00:10:13.601 --> 00:10:14.934
[ Laughter ]

00:10:14.934 --> 00:10:17.000
Guys, I saw it coming.
I didn't know how to stop it.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.601
[ Laughter ]

00:10:18.601 --> 00:10:20.334
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:20.334 --> 00:10:23.968
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

